INT. FUNERAL PARLOR BACK OFFICE - NIGHT

Wood paneling. Lilies in a vase. A desk lamp turned low. A phone sits on the blotter like a sleeping animal.

LAWRENCE "LARRY" PIETRZAK (50s, undertaker's black suit, tie loosened) counts bills at the desk. In the armchair sits his partner, VERONICA CHEN-ADEYEMI (40s, perfect posture, gloves on). On the sofa, a boy, MILO (teen, school blazer), turns an unlit candle over in his hands. At the window stands a figure, silent, looking out at the parking lot: TOBIAS WREN (30s, long coat).

The phone rings. Veronica lifts her eyes. Larry stops counting.

LARRY
Leave it.

VERONICA
It's the fourth time.

Larry's thumb works the edge of the bills. Milo sets the candle down.

MILO
Should I--

LARRY
No.

The phone rings. Rings. Rings. Wren turns from the window, watches the receiver, and picks it up without speaking. He listens. A thin voice crackles through.

CALLER (V.O.)
(over phone)
Is the arrangement still on for tomorrow?

Wren looks at Larry. Larry nods once.

WREN
(into phone)
It is.

He hangs up. Veronica unfolds her gloved hands, and, for the first time, Larry meets Milo's eyes.
